1. Ownership
   Except for third-party components, all rights in this software, including its
   source code, builds, visual design and documentation, belong to the copyright
   holder.

2. Permission
   You may run this software, as published by the copyright holder, in a web
   browser free of charge for any purpose, including commercial use. This covers
   the temporary copies a browser makes to run it.

3. Not permitted
   Except where the law allows it, you may not, without written permission of
   the copyright holder:
   (1) copy, modify, redistribute or make available all or part of this software;
   (2) sell, rent or sublicense this software;
   (3) remove or alter copyright or license notices.
   Being able to view the source code does not grant any of these rights.

4. Your work
   The copyright holder claims no rights in patches you create or in images you
   produce with this software. The bundled example patches may be used, modified
   and published freely in your own work, including commercially.

5. Third-party components
   Third-party components are governed by their own licenses, which take
   precedence over this document. They are listed in third-party-licenses.txt,
   distributed with this software.

6. No warranty and limitation of liability
   This software is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including operation, accuracy, fitness for a particular purpose and
   non-infringement. To the extent permitted by law, the copyright holder is not
   liable for damages arising from the use of, or inability to use, this
   software. This does not apply to intent, gross negligence, or any other case
   in which liability cannot be excluded by law.
